# Copy this file to tools/leaks.local.txt (which git ignores) and list what must never
# appear in a tracked file of this public repository.
#
# One regular expression per line, matched case-insensitively against every tracked
# file's path and text. Blank lines and lines starting with # are skipped.
#
# Do not commit the real list: a public repo that carried it would publish the names.
# In CI, put the same text in a repository secret named LEAKS_LIST; see
# the README section on the leak check.
#
# Examples (replace with your own):
\bExampleCorp\b
internal\.example\.test
